shmux/1.0.3@ohpcd/stable: Apply patch (portability): tests/run: point the analyzer script shebang at /data/service/hnp/bin/bash so the -A 2s analyzer timeout (child alarm before execvp) is not swallowed by hishell /bin/sh, which continues after SIGALRM and exits normally so 'Analyzer for N timed out' never fires; one line changed, no test case or assertion touched
shmux/1.0.3@ohpcd/stable: Apply patch (portability): analyzer.c: include pcreposix.h instead of the system regex.h so regcomp/regexec/regerror constants and compile-flag bit values match the linked libpcreposix (the conan pcre package injects -lpcreposix ahead of libc, so pcreposix provides the POSIX regex symbols): system regex.h has REG_NOMATCH=1/REG_EXTENDED=1/REG_NEWLINE=4/REG_NOSUB=8 while pcreposix uses REG_NOMATCH=17/REG_EXTENDED=0/REG_NEWLINE=0x0002/REG_NOSUB=0x0020, so every no-match was misread as a fatal error and every compile flag was reinterpreted; one line changed
